{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sxdn3pLVG6x1n4pDwwebJt","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t\n41\tThe build order in `docs/architecture.md` §12 is complete end to end for the CLI/eval\n42\tPOC: contract pin + stub emitter (M1), golden cases graded before the agent existed\n43\t(M2), the three tools/output union/rendering gate (M3), the frozen prompt and live eval\n44\ttier (M4), and the walked demo across its three modes (M5). Two things are carried but\n45\tintentionally **not** part of that MVP surface:\n46\t\n47\t- **The server layer is unwired (O-2).** A FastAPI scaffold lives under `server/`, but\n48\t  the product surface is CLI + evals; it is wired only when a demo needs a UI.\n49\t- **Forecasting is registered but gated (O-4, `VC-POC-14`).** One next-census School FTE\n50\t  forecast question is registered and `not_currently_supported` until it earns a passing\n51\t  local backtest; it is not part of MVP and a failed/blocked gate is a successful\n52\t  validation outcome, not a defect.\n53\t\n54\t## Live-eval checkpoints\n55\t\n56\t`python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)\n57\tafter each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format\n58\tversion, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and\n59\tthe saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\n60\trun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the\n61\tcontract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1.\n62\t\n63\t## Versioning\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50712efd-ac4a-4540-b086-5dbc582bfb74","uuid":"38d708c5-b613-4ece-8269-98eebfb4174e","timestamp":"2026-09-29T08:04:51.691Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/README.md","content":"\nThe build order in `docs/architecture.md` §12 is complete end to end for the CLI/eval\nPOC: contract pin + stub emitter (M1), golden cases graded before the agent existed\n(M2), the three tools/output union/rendering gate (M3), the frozen prompt and live eval\ntier (M4), and the walked demo across its three modes (M5). Two things are carried but\nintentionally **not** part of that MVP surface:\n\n- **The server layer is unwired (O-2).** A FastAPI scaffold lives under `server/`, but\n  the product surface is CLI + evals; it is wired only when a demo needs a UI.\n- **Forecasting is registered but gated (O-4, `VC-POC-14`).** One next-census School FTE\n  forecast question is registered and `not_currently_supported` until it earns a passing\n  local backtest; it is not part of MVP and a failed/blocked gate is a successful\n  validation outcome, not a defect.\n\n## Live-eval checkpoints\n\n`python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)\nafter each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format\nversion, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and\nthe saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\nrun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the\ncontract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1.\n\n## Versioning\n","numLines":25,"startLine":40,"totalLines":68}}}
