{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017RMJvPVdPznGxMRfovhtoq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50712efd-ac4a-4540-b086-5dbc582bfb74","uuid":"1340fec8-7daf-4948-b1a7-2195a2007441","timestamp":"2026-09-29T08:04:54.317Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/shane/Projects/k-12Harness/README.md","oldString":"the saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\nrun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the","newString":"the saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); on any mismatch the evaluator\n**refuses the `--resume` with an error rather than silently continuing under different\nterms or starting a fresh run itself** — it never starts a fresh run on your behalf, so\nthe operator must start a separate fresh run (drop `--resume`) explicitly. This is distinct from the","originalFile":"# K-12 Market Intelligence — Harness\n\nA natural-language harness over the deterministic evidence contract published by the\nK-12 data project. A PydanticAI agent maps a user's question to an approved question ID\nwith a validated structured request, invokes the data layer's emitter, and renders the\nreturned evidence envelope faithfully — confidence, provenance and limitations included,\nrefusals generated from the contract's own exclusion lists.\n\nThe harness never composes SQL, never touches a database, and never computes a figure.\n\n## Start here\n\n| Read | For |\n|---|---|\n| [`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md) | The system design — boundary, tools, output contract, eval design, build order |\n| [`docs/decisions.md`](docs/decisions.md) | The ADR log — **source of truth on any conflict** |\n| [`docs/prd.md`](docs/prd.md) + [`docs/prd-addendum.md`](docs/prd-addendum.md) | Product definition (carried verbatim from the planning phase) |\n| [`contract/`](contract/) | The pinned data-layer interface (registry, schemas, handoff, our change requests) |\n| [`HANDOVER.md`](HANDOVER.md) | What is built vs what the next session builds, in order |\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\nbash setup.sh                       # provision .venv from requirements.txt (idempotent)\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q   # unit tier: zero network, runs on every PR\n```\n\nConfiguration lives in `config/settings.py` — the single source of truth for model IDs,\nbudgets, cache minimums, and the data-project location (`DATA_PROJECT_ROOT`). The\n**default provider is `claude_account`** (ADR-019): the Claude CLI under subscription\nOAuth, invoked via `claude --print` with `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` inherited from the\nmachine-level environment — the token is never copied into this project's `.env` — and\npinned to model `claude-sonnet-4-6` (`config/settings.py` is the single source of truth\nfor that pin; it is not restated here as a literal that can drift). `anthropic_sdk` is\nan explicit, potentially metered opt-in, selected only with\n`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`; it is never the default. See `.env.example` and\n`RUNBOOK.md`.\n\n## Pipeline status (M1–M5)\n\nThe build order in `docs/architecture.md` §12 is complete end to end for the CLI/eval\nPOC: contract pin + stub emitter (M1), golden cases graded before the agent existed\n(M2), the three tools/output union/rendering gate (M3), the frozen prompt and live eval\ntier (M4), and the walked demo across its three modes (M5). Two things are carried but\nintentionally **not** part of that MVP surface:\n\n- **The server layer is unwired (O-2).** A FastAPI scaffold lives under `server/`, but\n  the product surface is CLI + evals; it is wired only when a demo needs a UI.\n- **Forecasting is registered but gated (O-4, `VC-POC-14`).** One next-census School FTE\n  forecast question is registered and `not_currently_supported` until it earns a passing\n  local backtest; it is not part of MVP and a failed/blocked gate is a successful\n  validation outcome, not a defect.\n\n## Live-eval checkpoints\n\n`python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)\nafter each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format\nversion, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and\nthe saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh\nrun rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the\ncontract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1.\n\n## Versioning\n\n`VERSION` is bumped by CI at merge — PRs never touch it. Each PR adds one\n`releases/_next/<slug>.md` (copy `releases/_template.md`); the contract is in\n`releases/README.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":56,"oldLines":8,"newStart":56,"newLines":10,"lines":[" `python -m evals.live` writes a resumable checkpoint (`logs/eval/live-<timestamp>.json`)"," after each trial. A saved checkpoint may be **resumed only when its report format"," version, its contract version, its model and its stage all match the current run, and","-the saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); any mismatch starts a fresh","-run rather than silently continuing under different terms. This is distinct from the","+the saved case selection still exists** (`evals/live.py`); on any mismatch the evaluator","+**refuses the `--resume` with an error rather than silently continuing under different","+terms or starting a fresh run itself** — it never starts a fresh run on your behalf, so","+the operator must start a separate fresh run (drop `--resume`) explicitly. This is distinct from the"," contract hash pin (ADR-008) and the SDK+framework pin (ADR-015-3) — see `RUNBOOK.md` §1."," "," ## Versioning"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true}}
